{"term":"beam","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b75358e4b3da881707","definition":"Any large piece of timber or iron long in proportion to its thickness, and prepared for use.","example":"And a letter vnto Asaph the keeper of the kings forrest, that he may giue me timber to make beames for the gates of the palace which appertained to the house, and for the wall of the Citie, and for the house that I shall enter into: And the king granted me, according to the good hand of my God vpon me.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abeam","airbeam","Airy beam","balance beam","beamage","beam and scales","beambird","beambreak","Beam Bridge","beam compass","beam-ends","beam engine","beamer","beamform","beamformed","beamformer","beamforming","beamful","beam hole","beamish","beamless","beamlet","beamlike","beamline","beam-on","beampattern","beampipe","beam reach","beam sea","beamshelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d56594edfb146657ab","definition":"One of the principal horizontal structural members, usually of steel, timber, or concrete, of a building.","example":"The brasswork here, how rich it is in beams, / And how, besides, it makes the whole house sound.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abeam","airbeam","Airy beam","balance beam","beamage","beam and scales","beambird","beambreak","Beam Bridge","beam compass","beam-ends","beam engine","beamer","beamform","beamformed","beamformer","beamforming","beamful","beam hole","beamish","beamless","beamlet","beamlike","beamline","beam-on","beampattern","beampipe","beam reach","beam sea","beamshelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:712a81cf54f3637aaa","definition":"One of the transverse members of a ship's frame on which the decks are laid, and acting as part of the support for keeping the sides of the vessel in shape — supported at the sides by knees in wooden ships and by stringers in steel ones; cf. abeam, beam-ends.","example":"Capt. King, from Demarara, was invaded by the gale on the evening of the 6th, in lat. 21° 51', and his vessel was thrown on her beam ends. He was forced to cut away her main-mast. Lost a man, who was washed overboard.\n. . .\nCapt. Mood, on a voyage from Alexandria (Virginia), to St. Mary's (Georgia), was, on the night of the 7th, in the Gulf Stream, to the eastward of Charlston: the wind there was east-north-east, and so hard as to throw his vessel on her beam ends. She lay several hours in this situation. Several of his crew were washed overboard.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abeam","airbeam","Airy beam","balance beam","beamage","beam and scales","beambird","beambreak","Beam Bridge","beam compass","beam-ends","beam engine","beamer","beamform","beamformed","beamformer","beamforming","beamful","beam hole","beamish","beamless","beamlet","beamlike","beamline","beam-on","beampattern","beampipe","beam reach","beam sea","beamshelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c66ecd4bdc33bc04c6","definition":"The maximum width of a vessel (note that a vessel with a beam of 15 foot can also be said to be 15 foot abeam).","example":"This ship has more beam than that one.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["breadth"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abeam","airbeam","Airy beam","balance beam","beamage","beam and scales","beambird","beambreak","Beam Bridge","beam compass","beam-ends","beam engine","beamer","beamform","beamformed","beamformer","beamforming","beamful","beam hole","beamish","beamless","beamlet","beamlike","beamline","beam-on","beampattern","beampipe","beam reach","beam sea","beamshelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:60f70ab89654879e6c","definition":"The direction across a vessel, perpendicular to fore-and-aft.","example":"As the vessel passes a landmark, the landmark is said to be abeam. Once the vessel has passed the landmark, it falls abaft the beam, then it gradually falls astern.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abeam","airbeam","Airy beam","balance beam","beamage","beam and scales","beambird","beambreak","Beam Bridge","beam compass","beam-ends","beam engine","beamer","beamform","beamformed","beamformer","beamforming","beamful","beam hole","beamish","beamless","beamlet","beamlike","beamline","beam-on","beampattern","beampipe","beam reach","beam sea","beamshelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2c35d62e8382cee134","definition":"The straight part or shank of an anchor.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abeam","airbeam","Airy beam","balance beam","beamage","beam and scales","beambird","beambreak","Beam Bridge","beam compass","beam-ends","beam engine","beamer","beamform","beamformed","beamformer","beamforming","beamful","beam hole","beamish","beamless","beamlet","beamlike","beamline","beam-on","beampattern","beampipe","beam reach","beam sea","beamshelf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beam#E